@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@ Part of [`ROADMAP.md`](../ROADMAP.md). The to-do milestones of this part (M11 Ne
 
 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-25 (9): a bed tapped by day says "You can only sleep at night" (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; no test, `use_bed` needs the whole `App`). `EntityPlayer.sleepInBedAt` answers NOT_POSSIBLE_NOW by day and `BlockBed.blockActivated` shows `tile.bed.noSleep`; `use_bed` returned silently. The one-line message of the pack (`hint`, 2.5 s, lower middle) now carries its text in `hint_msg`, so the bed reuses it (a live, awake player only, as vanilla's order of checks).
+    - ponytail: no other status message (too far, monsters near). UNVERIFIED: the wording (the lang file, from memory), that it compiles (two fields set by one tuple assignment, `hint_msg` read in the HUD pass beside `v`).
 - 2026-10-25 (8): organic mob movement from `EntityLiving` (b1.7.3 decompiled), every mob, closer to b1.7.3 and not away from it; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +3 tests `mobs::tests::{a_mob_eases_into_a_walk_and_glides_to_a_stop, the_body_trails_the_head_and_follows_the_walk, a_mob_looking_at_the_player_tips_its_head_toward_their_eyes}`; run `cargo test --lib mobs items` first. What was stiff: the walk speed was set outright every frame (a mob started and stopped at full speed and a hop lost its run), the body pointed where `yaw` pointed, and `yaw` moves in 20 Hz steps (up to 30 degrees at once), so every turn was a jerk.
     - Momentum (`Mob::step`): `vel = target + (vel - target) x keep`, `keep` = 0.546^ticks on the ground, 0.91^ticks in the air (the drags of `moveEntityWithHeading`); under 0.02 m/s it stops. In water or lava the old direct set stays (`step_box` scales the swim speed by itself). Knockback (`free`) and the squid's own swim are untouched.
     - `body_yaw` (`renderYawOffset`): moving faster than 0.05 blocks a tick (and not knocked back) it eases to the heading of the move by 0.3 of the gap a tick; then it is held within 75 degrees of `yaw`. `render/items.rs` draws the body with it and turns the head (and a hen's beak) by `mobs::lead(yaw, body_yaw)` about its own pivot. The sign of that turn in the mirrored model space is worked out, not seen.
